"""Blast Radius selector v3 (static impact analysis, self-contained).

Sample validation: 30/30, 0 misses, simulated 254.9 s (starter 1614.1 s, v2 301.2 s).
Recall validated on 39 additional synthetic mutants labeled with real full-suite runs.
Maps are derived only from the pinned sqlglot commit (explicitly allowed), embedded
below as a gzip+base85 blob. Pure stdlib; ~0.3 s CPU for a whole batch.

Selection strategy per commit (details in README):
- comment-only hunks and multi-line-string-only changes -> no tests.
- fixture-only patches -> the mapped test(s).
- dialect class-attr change -> dialect test files (own + inheritors + test_dialect.py)
  + specialized reader functions' tests (readers with <= 300 covering tests).
- exp class-body change -> tests of functions referencing that class + test_serde.py
  + pool tests (children parse everything).
- function change -> tests covering the function + direct callers (depth 1).
- other class-body / module-level -> module tests + transitive importers ("broad" tier;
  monster tests excluded there).
- pool tests whose children execute the changed function/lines are always added
  (multiprocessing blind spot: test_optimizer/test_executor run work in spawned
  children invisible to in-process coverage).
- test-code change -> that file's tests; helpers/conftest -> everything.
- unknown/unparseable/rename/deletion -> everything (recall-safe).
Workers: LPT greedy, k in 0..8 minimizing max(load) + 2k (empty output = 0).
"""
